  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration is config_042 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. In singleprofile settings, weighted fusion marginally outperformed concat (0.537 vs 0.532), but that difference was small. In the multiprofile regime—where performance gains are largest—we have only tested weighted fusion (config_042, config_046). The effect of fusion strategy in multiprofile is therefore untested. Question: config_013 is identical to config_042 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, isolating the fusion effect under the strongest-performing multiprofile + transformer aggregation setup. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against the current best, directly testing whether the fusion choice that showed only a marginal edge in singleprofile also matters (or even reverses) when multiprofile + transformer aggregation is in play. If concat matches or beats weighted, it broadens the design space at no cost; if weighted clearly wins, we confirm the fusion choice and can confidently move budget toward testing alternative RNA encoders or image encoders in the multiprofile setting. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

